! The hole ender of `phrasing.xfst`: the verb of the clause is the word written
! next, so the clause is stroked first and the word after it.
!
! Its own directory, and not part of `tests/golden/phrasing.tsv`, because what a
! golden file asks is what one outline means and what these ask is what two of
! them write together. The inflection is `{:infl:…}`, a lexicon, so this needs
! `build/morph` and `check.sh` skips it where those are absent.
!
! `scripts/check-hold.py` replays every case here through a real Plover engine
! and compares, so each line is two hosts' answer.

! ---- the verb hole, `-RG`, over the corners of the clause
!buffer
+T-RG
RUPB
!buffer
+T-RGD
RUPB
!buffer
+TERG
RUPB
!buffer
+TURG
RUPB

! A modal takes the base form, so the hole asks for nothing at all and the word
! stands as it was written.
!buffer
+TARG
RUPB

! The passive, the negative and the question, which are the same corners a verb
! of its own would take.
!buffer
+PH-RG
RUPB
!buffer
+K*RG
RUPB
!buffer
#+T-RG
RUPB

! An irregular, which is why the tail is a lexicon and not a rule.
!buffer
+T-RGD
TKPW
!buffer
+TURG
TKPW

! ---- the adverb ender, which carries the hole always
! An adverb inflects for nothing, so a clause ending on one has no verb for its
! tense or aspect to inflect either: the word written next is that verb, and no
! key says so. `-D` is the tense it is everywhere else, which is a past the
! launchpad never had.
!buffer
+T-FBTS
RUPB
!buffer
+T-FBTSD
RUPB
!buffer
+TEFBTS
RUPB
!buffer
+TEFBTSD
RUPB
!buffer
+T*FBTS
RUPB
!buffer
+T-RGTS
KAER

! The passive of an adverb ender was no clause at all, and now it is one.
!buffer
+PH-FBTS
WREU

! An infinitive keeps the adverb and takes the verb, where it used to drop the
! adverb and write "be".
!buffer
+HR-FBTS
RUPB

! ---- what the hole displaced
!buffer
+T-RGT
!buffer
+T-RPGT
